From 8311d8f8273db0eab8fd7a46e7cd1397423e8359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 18:30:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(inbox): bounded collectInbox + accumulation-safe
 UserPromptSubmit nudge (CodeRabbit #379)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MAJOR (inbox.js perf): collectInbox now (1) accepts a cached opts.dashboardInboxId
(may be null to skip the board tier) so hot paths avoid re-scanning the full issue
list every call, and (2) early-terminates the sequential per-issue comment I/O once
pending reaches the limit. Targeting semantics (fail-closed session/worktree/actor)
are unchanged — only the lowest-priority tail is skipped.

MINOR (hooks.js stability): UserPromptSubmit additionalContext ACCUMULATES across
prompts (documented Claude Code limitation), so re-emitting full fenced bodies each
prompt bloats context. The recurring UPS tier now emits a compact count+pointer nudge
(buildInboxNudge, no untrusted bodies); the full fenced digest stays on SessionStart
(inboxSection) + `forge inbox`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
